<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <script>
      (function () {
        try {
          var t = localStorage.getItem("theme");
          if (t !== "light" && t !== "dark") {
            t = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
          }
          document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", t);
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Whoami – one link for all of you" %></title>
    <meta name="description" content="<%= content_for(:description) || "One page you own: name, work, links, writing. The link for your email signature, your bios, your slides." %>">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#F3F3F1" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0C0C0C" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
    <% if content_for?(:canonical) %>
      <link rel="canonical" href="<%= content_for(:canonical) %>">
      <meta property="og:url" content="<%= content_for(:canonical) %>">
    <% end %>
    <meta property="og:title" content="<%= content_for(:title) || "Whoami – one link for all of you" %>">
    <meta property="og:description" content="<%= content_for(:description) || "One page you own: name, work, links, writing. The link for your email signature, your bios, your slides." %>">
    <meta property="og:type" content="<%= content_for(:og_type) || "website" %>">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%= yield :head %>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png">
    <%= render "shared/fonts" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "lexxy", "theme_defaults", "theme_toggle", "actiontext", "profile", "landing", "gate", "workspace", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>
  <body class="<%= content_for(:body_class) %>">
    <!--
      whoami · direction contract (Poster)
      THESIS: A person's page is a poster — one name set huge, everything else in order beneath it. Refuses the button stack and the fixed grid; every section is exactly as tall as its content, so a thin page still reads as finished.
      OWN-WORLD: The app's own canvas (soft grey, near-black in dark) and ink type; Bricolage Grotesque at 7rem for the name, Geist body, Geist Mono for handles/dates/hosts; links as a hairline index with brand-coloured glyph discs (the only colour besides the green current-role date in Work); Work and Writing as chapters with display headings and hairline rows. Landing, dashboard, gate and email share the same canvas and ink actions.
      STORY: Visitor gets the name and the one-line bio in one glance, then scans the index to find the person elsewhere, then the ledger to see what they did and wrote. Owner edits in a workshop that previews the same page live, drafts included.
      FIRST VIEWPORT: Name at 7rem, handle in mono under it, bio (photo at right on desktop, first and centred on mobile), then the first link rows. Primary action on landing: the claim form + "Create yours" in ink.
      FORM: Poster; seed: none — direction pinned by the user from four content-height options after the mosaic proved weak on thin pages.
      FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
    -->
    <%= render FlashComponent.new(notice:, alert:) %>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
